{%- render 'section-design', section: section -%}
{{ 'sj-pdp.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<script src="{{ 'sj-pdp.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
{%- comment -%}
  Product detail — the designed three-column page, rendered from the real
  product on the server.

  Everything the shopper reads about the piece is the merchant's own data: title,
  price and compare-at from the selected variant, the gallery from product.media,
  the description in the first accordion, and the four editable metafields in the
  `shrujan` namespace (craft, badge, swatches — occasion has no slot in this
  design). The rails are real collections.

  What stays a section setting is the copy the design repeats on every piece and
  that was never product data: the intro line, the "Made with" pills, the
  care/shipping accordions, the ordering options, and the review panel (reviews
  are blocks, so they stay editable).

  Add to bag is a real POST to the cart, so the built cart page receives it. The
  size row switches the posted variant when the product has real options; when it
  has only Shopify's default variant the row is presentational and the default
  variant is what gets added.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Gallery layout. The ≤720px stylesheet already lays the thumbnail rail out
  under the shot, so "below" simply asks for that arrangement at every width;
  and the pinned block is released by returning .pdp__media to static, which is
  what it already becomes at ≤1080px. Both are written only when the merchant
  moves off the built design.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign cfg = section.settings
  assign root_sel = '#shopify-section-' | append: section.id

  comment
    Mobile group. Two different breakpoints already own the gallery, and neither
    is invented here: 1080px is where the stylesheet stops pinning the block, and
    720px is where it moves the thumbnail rail under the shot as a sideways strip
    and drops the stage to min(64vh, 520px). So the phone controls are that same
    720px tier — whether the strip is worth its room, and what the stage's height
    should be, which also has to beat the taller height "below" publishes without
    a query of its own. The four maker portraits and the review columns are real
    grids that never step; the reviews stack at 720px, the portraits never do.

    There is no phone switch for un-pinning: the stylesheet has already released
    the block by 1080px, so a phone would never see it pinned.
  endcomment
  assign pdp_style = false
  if cfg.gallery_thumbs != 'left' or cfg.gallery_sticky == false
    assign pdp_style = true
  endif
  if cfg.gallery_thumbs_m != 'strip' or cfg.gallery_h_m != 0
    assign pdp_style = true
  endif
  if cfg.faces_cols_m != 4 or cfg.reviews_cols_m != 1
    assign pdp_style = true
  endif
  if cfg.show_reviews and cfg.show_reviews_m == false
    assign pdp_style = true
  endif
  if cfg.show_rec and cfg.show_rec_m == false
    assign pdp_style = true
  endif
  if cfg.show_other and cfg.show_other_m == false
    assign pdp_style = true
  endif
-%}
{%- if pdp_style -%}
  <style>
    {%- if cfg.gallery_thumbs == 'below' -%}
      {{ root_sel }} .pdp__media { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
      {{ root_sel }} .pdp__rail {
        order: 2;
        grid-auto-flow: column;
        grid-auto-columns: 64px;
        overflow-x: auto;
        scrollbar-width: none;
        padding-top: 10px;
      }
      {{ root_sel }} .pdp__rail::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none; }
      {%- comment -%}
        The stage is sized to fill the screen, so with the rail moved underneath
        it the pinned block has to give back the strip's height (a 64px-wide
        thumbnail at 3/4 is ~85px tall, plus its 10px of padding) or the
        thumbnails would sit below the fold of the block that pins them.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {{ root_sel }} .pdp__stage {
        order: 1;
        height: min(calc(100vh - 2 * clamp(14px, 1.6vw, 26px) - 104px), 756px);
      }
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if cfg.gallery_sticky == false -%}
      {{ root_sel }} .pdp__media { position: static; }
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Phone. Coming after the block above is what lets the stage height here beat
      the un-mediated one "thumbnails below" writes.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if cfg.gallery_thumbs_m != 'strip' or cfg.gallery_h_m != 0 or cfg.faces_cols_m != 4 or cfg.reviews_cols_m != 1 -%}
      @media (max-width: 720px) {
        {%- if cfg.gallery_thumbs_m == 'hidden' -%}
          {{ root_sel }} .pdp__rail { display: none; }
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if cfg.gallery_h_m != 0 -%}
          {{ root_sel }} .pdp__stage { height: {{ cfg.gallery_h_m }}px; }
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if cfg.faces_cols_m != 4 -%}
          {{ root_sel }} .pdp__faces { grid-template-columns: repeat({{ cfg.faces_cols_m }}, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if cfg.reviews_cols_m != 1 -%}
          {{ root_sel }} .reviews { grid-template-columns: repeat({{ cfg.reviews_cols_m }}, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
        {%- endif -%}
      }
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if cfg.show_reviews_m == false or cfg.show_rec_m == false or cfg.show_other_m == false -%}
      @media (max-width: 720px) {
        {%- if cfg.show_reviews and cfg.show_reviews_m == false -%}
          {{ root_sel }} .pdp-reviews { display: none; }
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if cfg.show_rec and cfg.show_rec_m == false -%}
          {{ root_sel }} .pdp-rec { display: none; }
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if cfg.show_other and cfg.show_other_m == false -%}
          {{ root_sel }} .pdp-other { display: none; }
        {%- endif -%}
      }
    {%- endif -%}
  </style>
{%- endif -%}
{%- liquid
  comment
    The piece itself, from Shopify. The variant the page quotes and adds is the
    one Shopify has selected, or the first that can be bought.
  endcomment
  assign variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  if variant == blank
    assign variant = product.variants.first
  endif

  assign craft = product.metafields.shrujan.craft.value
  if craft == blank
    assign craft = product.type
  endif

  comment
    The badge is decided by snippets/piece-badge.liquid, the same rules the grids
    use: sold out wins the one corner the design drew, then the discount worked
    out from the prices, then the shrujan.badge override.
  endcomment

  comment
    The swatch discs the shrujan.swatches metafield feeds are a card affordance —
    the designed buying column has no colour row, so the pieces on the rails below
    are where a product's colours are drawn.
  endcomment
  assign has_was = false
  if variant.compare_at_price > variant.price
    assign has_was = true
  endif

  comment
    The gallery is the image media in the order the merchant arranged it.
  endcomment
  assign shots = product.media | where: 'media_type', 'image'
  assign shot_count = shots.size
  if shot_count > cfg.gallery_max
    assign shot_count = cfg.gallery_max
  endif

  comment
    Sizes are the product's own: when it carries the option, each button is a
    variant and picking it changes what the form posts. A product with only
    Shopify's default variant has no size to choose, so the row is not drawn.
    A bag or a cushion cover offering XS to XXL was the prototype talking.
  endcomment
  assign size_pos = 0
  for opt in product.options_with_values
    assign opt_name = opt.name | downcase | strip
    if opt_name == 'size' or opt_name == 'sizes'
      assign size_list = opt.values
      assign size_pos = forloop.index
      break
    endif
  endfor
  if size_pos == 0 and product.has_only_default_variant == false
    assign first_opt = product.options_with_values | first
    assign size_list = first_opt.values
    assign size_pos = 1
  endif

  assign from_variants = true
  if size_pos == 0
    assign from_variants = false
  else
    case size_pos
      when 1
        assign current_size = variant.option1
      when 2
        assign current_size = variant.option2
      else
        assign current_size = variant.option3
    endcase
  endif

  assign spec_list = cfg.specs | strip | newline_to_br | split: '<br />'

  comment
    The star row is the rating rounded to whole stars; an unreadable rating keeps
    the five the design was drawn with.
  endcomment
  assign star_n = cfg.rating | plus: 0 | round
  if star_n < 1 or star_n > 5
    assign star_n = 5
  endif

  assign shop_url = cfg.shop_link | default: '/pages/shop-shrujan'

  comment
    The same-hands rail is the product's own group: product.type carries the
    collection name the catalogue was built from, so its handle addresses the
    same rail the design showed. Anything unfamiliar falls back to everything.
  endcomment
  assign type_handle = product.type | handleize
  assign rec_coll = collections[type_handle]
  unless rec_coll.products.size > 0
    assign rec_coll = collections['all']
  endunless
  comment
    The lower rail must not repeat what the upper one just showed, so both walk
    one `shown` list, delimited so `dupatta` cannot match `dupatta-copy`.
  endcomment
  assign shown = '|' | append: product.handle | append: '|'
  assign rail_max = 5
-%}
